[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Schema [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mWhat should the preferences module store, and how strict should it be?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mFixed schema + defaults (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mDeclared keys with typed defaults and validation. Start with rememberedUsername and theme. Corrupt storage falls [39m
     [38;5;246mback to defaults.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Fixed schema, rememberedUsername only
     [38;5;246mSame validated approach, but only the one preference the login form actually needs. Smallest honest scope.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Generic key-value store
     [38;5;246mAny JSON-serializable value under any key, no schema or defaults. Flexible, but callers handle validation [39m
     [38;5;246mthemselves.[39m
